00:57:14.370 --> 00:57:19.350
And that's so they can get your dialogue clean and so that they can cut between different takes.
这样是为了保证台词清晰，也方便在不同拍摄片段之间剪辑。

1471
00:57:19.350 --> 00:57:21.630
And it, you don't want this song in the background.
你肯定不希望背景里一直响着那首歌。

1472
00:57:21.990 --> 00:57:27.810
Well, for this scene, they actually played the music on the boombox.
不过这场戏，他们确实在片场用收音机播放了音乐。

1473
00:57:28.030 --> 00:57:31.870
And it made for a bit of a challenge in the editing room.
这给剪辑室带来了一些挑战。

1474
00:57:32.050 --> 00:57:38.490
But Greg felt like it provided so much to Rain's performance.
但格雷格觉得这给雷恩的表演增色不少。

1475
00:57:38.490 --> 00:57:39.250
Performance, yeah.
确实是表演。

1476
00:57:39.410 --> 00:57:41.930
For him to have that music blaring.
让他伴着震耳欲聋的音乐表演。

1477
00:57:42.310 --> 00:57:43.970
And also, it's documentary.
而且这是纪录片风格。

1478
00:57:43.970 --> 00:57:49.950
So you wouldn't have this, like, clean track of the music playing later.
所以后期不可能有那种干净的音乐音轨。

1479
00:57:50.170 --> 00:57:51.970
Although we did in Cafe Disco.
虽然我们在拍“迪斯科咖啡馆”那集时确实有。

1480
00:57:52.110 --> 00:57:53.510
We all had to dance to nothing.
我们当时都得对着空气跳舞。

1481
00:57:53.510 --> 00:57:53.930
I remember that.
我记得那次。

1482
00:57:54.030 --> 00:57:54.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1483
00:57:54.610 --> 00:57:57.850
In the little Michael Scott paper company thing.
就在那个小小的迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司里。

1484
00:57:58.050 --> 00:57:58.390
All right.
好的。

1485
00:57:58.450 --> 00:58:00.910
So now we move into Michael's office.
现在我们转到迈克尔的办公室。

1486
00:58:01.130 --> 00:58:06.050
And Dwight is going to give his pitch for why he deserves a raise.
德怀特要开始陈述他为什么应该加薪了。

1487
00:58:06.310 --> 00:58:06.570
Okay.
好的。

1488
00:58:06.650 --> 00:58:09.450
This scene happens at around 17 minutes, 14 seconds.
这场戏大约发生在17分14秒处。

1489
00:58:09.450 --> 00:58:12.990
I just have to tell you guys, I did a lot of scenes with Rainn Wilson.
我得告诉你们，我和雷恩·威尔森拍过很多对手戏。

1490
00:58:13.470 --> 00:58:15.710
And here's something you have to know about him.
关于他，你们必须知道一件事。

1491
00:58:16.050 --> 00:58:18.130
The man loves a prop.
这家伙特别喜欢用道具。

1492
00:58:18.410 --> 00:58:20.850
He loves a prop, guys.
他真的很爱用道具，伙计们。

1493
00:58:20.870 --> 00:58:21.210
He does.
确实如此。

1494
00:58:21.390 --> 00:58:22.310
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1495
00:58:22.410 --> 00:58:25.370
So it was no surprise to me when he held up that binder.
所以当他举起那个活页夹时，我一点也不惊讶。

1496
00:58:25.590 --> 00:58:29.730
I have a feeling him and Phil Shea talked a lot about that binder and what would go in it.
我有种预感，他和道具师菲尔·谢伊肯定为了那个活页夹以及里面放什么东西讨论了很久。

1497
00:58:29.810 --> 00:58:31.410
But Rainn loves a prop.
但雷恩就是爱用道具。

1498
00:58:31.410 --> 00:58:38.110
Well, you can see at 18 minutes, 12 seconds, speaking of props, there is a sign.
说到道具，你们可以在18分12秒看到那里有个标牌。

1499
00:58:38.350 --> 00:58:38.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1500
00:58:39.170 --> 00:58:42.670
And it never gets referred to in the scene because it got deleted.
但那场戏里从来没提到过它，因为它被删减了。

1501
00:58:43.190 --> 00:58:47.050
Dwight has made a sign of himself where he breaks down his name.
德怀特给自己做了一个牌子，上面把他的名字拆解开了。

1502
00:58:47.230 --> 00:58:48.190
I wrote it all down.
我全都记下来了。

1503
00:58:48.210 --> 00:58:49.230
I did, too.
我也记了。

1504
00:58:49.450 --> 00:58:49.910
Okay, say it, Ange.
好吧，安吉，你说吧。

1505
00:58:49.910 --> 00:58:50.810
Let's take turns.
我们轮流来吧。

1506
00:58:50.970 --> 00:58:51.590
You do the first one.
你先说第一个。

1507
00:58:51.690 --> 00:58:52.550
Well, let's go back and forth.
嗯，我们交替着来吧。

1508
00:58:52.730 --> 00:58:52.870
Okay.
好。

1509
00:58:53.050 --> 00:58:54.610
Dwight's acronym for his name.
德怀特名字的首字母缩写。

1510
00:58:55.450 --> 00:58:55.930
Determined.
意志坚定（Determined）。

1511
00:58:56.330 --> 00:58:56.810
Worker.
工作者（Worker）。

1512
00:58:57.750 --> 00:58:58.230
Intense.
专注（Intense）。

1513
00:58:59.030 --> 00:58:59.810
Good worker.
好员工（Good worker）。

1514
00:59:00.230 --> 00:59:01.030
Hard worker.
勤奋（Hard worker）。

1515
00:59:01.030 --> 00:59:01.810
Terrific.
了不起（Terrific）。

1516
00:59:03.660 --> 00:59:09.760
You actually, I have to advise people to go back and watch the deleted scenes from this
其实，我得建议大家回去看看这一集的删减片段，

1517
00:59:09.760 --> 00:59:13.480
because there is a whole scene where he explains this.
因为里面有一整段戏是他解释这个缩写的。

1518
00:59:14.340 --> 00:59:17.300
First, he explains it to Jim at their desks.
首先，他在办公桌前向吉姆解释了一遍。

1519
00:59:17.380 --> 00:59:22.760
And then he makes suggestions for what Jim's acronym could be.
然后他还给吉姆的名字想了几个缩写建议。

1520
00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:23.880
He does?
真的吗？

1521
00:59:24.080 --> 00:59:24.340
Yes.
是的。

1522
00:59:24.460 --> 00:59:25.320
And it's really good.
而且非常精彩。

1523
00:59:25.500 --> 00:59:30.020
And then they also show the scene from Michael's office.
之后他们还放了迈克尔办公室里的那段戏。

1524
00:59:30.020 --> 00:59:31.100
So it's good stuff.
所以内容很棒。

1525
00:59:31.100 --> 00:59:36.100
It is interesting to me that the two characters that were the most excited about their performance
我觉得很有意思的一点是，对绩效评估最兴奋的两个角色，

1526
00:59:36.100 --> 00:59:37.520
review were Dwight and Angela.
分别是德怀特和安吉拉。

1527
00:59:38.180 --> 00:59:42.460
I mean, Dwight put so much effort into his, and then all Michael said was he's adequate.
我是说，德怀特在上面花了很多心思，结果迈克尔只说了句他表现尚可。

1528
00:59:42.820 --> 00:59:45.740
And then my character is like, I love to be judged.
而我的角色当时是说，我喜欢被评价。

1529
00:59:45.800 --> 00:59:48.100
I think I hold up even to the most severe scrutiny.
我觉得我经得起最严苛的审视。

1530
00:59:48.260 --> 00:59:49.440
I'm so excited for this.
我对此感到非常兴奋。

1531
00:59:49.580 --> 00:59:52.220
And then he just slams the door in my face and says, you're satisfactory.
结果他直接把门甩在我脸上，说我表现合格。

1532
00:59:52.800 --> 00:59:53.700
Oh, I know.
噢，我知道。

1533
00:59:53.800 --> 00:59:54.460
It's so sad.
太可怜了。

1534
00:59:54.460 --> 00:59:58.020
But the two people who really wanted a performance review don't get it.
但这两个真正想要绩效评估的人却没得到。

1535
00:59:58.200 --> 01:00:00.960
So around 18 minutes, Jan is fed up.
大约在18分钟左右，简受够了。

1536
01:00:01.120 --> 01:00:01.680
She's like, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1537
01:00:01.680 --> 01:00:02.360
I need a minute.
我需要一分钟。

1538
01:00:02.540 --> 01:00:03.500
I'm going to step out.
我要出去一下。

1539
01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:04.780
I'm going to collect my thoughts.
我要整理一下思绪。

1540
01:00:04.960 --> 01:00:06.360
And she goes into the hallway.
于是她走到了走廊里。

1541
01:00:06.360 --> 01:00:08.600
And we see the sign for the building.
我们看到了大楼的指示牌。

1542
01:00:08.740 --> 01:00:10.820
And here's what's in the building that we see.
这就是我们看到的大楼里的信息。

1543
01:00:11.280 --> 01:00:12.000
W.B.
W.B.

1544
01:00:12.160 --> 01:00:13.200
Jones Heating and Air.
琼斯供暖与空调公司。

1545
01:00:13.200 --> 01:00:15.340
That's in Office 110.
那是在110办公室。

1546
01:00:16.540 --> 01:00:17.960
Available 1,400.
可用面积1400。

1547
01:00:18.360 --> 01:00:19.820
It's available space.
那是可用空间。

1548
01:00:20.160 --> 01:00:21.440
And then the number is 120.
然后号码是120。

1549
01:00:21.860 --> 01:00:21.940
What?
什么？

1550
01:00:22.380 --> 01:00:23.940
Then we have Dunder Mifflin, Inc.
然后我们看到了邓德·米夫林公司。

1551
01:00:24.220 --> 01:00:25.080
Suite 200.
200号套房。

1552
01:00:25.200 --> 01:00:27.840
And then we have Vance Refrigeration, Suite 210.
然后是210号套房的万斯制冷公司。

1553
01:00:28.660 --> 01:00:30.280
So here's something that's interesting.
所以这里有个有趣的地方。

1554
01:00:31.460 --> 01:00:36.520
We haven't done that episode where we meet all the people in the business park yet.
我们还没拍过那一集，就是介绍商业园区里所有人的那一集。

1555
01:00:36.820 --> 01:00:38.640
But they had to make that prop.
但他们必须制作那个道具。

1556
01:00:39.040 --> 01:00:39.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1557
01:00:39.860 --> 01:00:41.140
So I want to ask.
所以我想问问。

1558
01:00:41.360 --> 01:00:42.780
That would actually be set deck.
那其实应该是布景组负责的。

1559
01:00:42.780 --> 01:00:44.440
I want to ask Michael Gallenberg.
我想问问迈克尔·加伦伯格。

1560
01:00:44.680 --> 01:00:47.320
Did he just randomly make up that J.B.
他是随口编出了那个J.B.

1561
01:00:47.980 --> 01:00:48.440
whatever?
什么的吗？

1562
01:00:48.880 --> 01:00:49.240
WB.
WB。

1563
01:00:49.360 --> 01:00:50.020
The WB.
WB电视台。

1564
01:00:50.240 --> 01:00:52.000
And did he make up Vance Refrigeration?
还有他是编出了万斯制冷公司吗？

1565
01:00:52.120 --> 01:00:52.780
WB Jones.
WB琼斯。

1566
01:00:53.020 --> 01:00:57.980
I mean, Vance Refrigeration is put there so far before we ever deal with it.
我是说，万斯制冷公司在我们要处理相关剧情很久之前就放在那儿了。

1567
01:00:58.040 --> 01:00:59.540
I wonder, like, what that was.
我很好奇，那到底是怎么回事。

1568
01:00:59.540 --> 01:01:00.400
Who came up with that?
是谁想出来的？

1569
01:01:00.460 --> 01:01:00.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1570
01:01:00.700 --> 01:01:05.560
We need to talk to Michael about all of those little things because they will come to figure
我们需要和迈克尔聊聊所有这些小细节，因为它们后来变得

1571
01:01:05.560 --> 01:01:08.060
so prominently in upcoming episodes.
在后续剧集中非常重要。

1572
01:01:08.060 --> 01:01:08.740
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1573
01:01:08.860 --> 01:01:10.080
Bob Vance, for example.
比如鲍勃·万斯。

1574
01:01:10.200 --> 01:01:10.250
Bob Vance.
鲍勃·万斯。

1575
01:01:10.250 --> 01:01:11.180
Vance Refrigeration.
万斯制冷公司。

1576
01:01:11.180 --> 01:01:14.280
Then we have the scene with Jim and Pam in the break room.
然后是吉姆和帕姆在休息室的那场戏。

1577
01:01:14.460 --> 01:01:14.880
Yes.
没错。

1578
01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.540
They're talking about Michael and Jan.
他们在谈论迈克尔和简。

1579
01:01:17.140 --> 01:01:20.240
And Pam says, how do you come back from that?
帕姆说，那种事之后怎么还能像以前一样相处？

1580
01:01:20.900 --> 01:01:27.080
And Jim so clearly takes it to heart because he's thinking, how would they come back if
吉姆显然往心里去了，因为他在想，如果他和帕姆

1581
01:01:27.080 --> 01:01:29.260
him and Pam hooked up and it didn't work out?
好上了但最后没成，他们该怎么面对彼此？

1582
01:01:29.300 --> 01:01:30.100
How would they come back?
他们该怎么面对彼此？

1583
01:01:30.200 --> 01:01:31.280
How would he come back from that?
他该怎么面对那种局面？

1584
01:01:31.480 --> 01:01:33.540
It's so clear to me that that's what he's thinking.
我非常确定他当时就是这么想的。

1585
01:01:33.540 --> 01:01:37.740
And he's like, yeah, you know, I don't know how you do come back from that, especially if
他说，是啊，你知道，我不知道那种事之后怎么还能像以前一样，尤其是

1586
01:01:37.740 --> 01:01:38.420
you work together.
你们还在同一个办公室工作。

1587
01:01:38.800 --> 01:01:40.500
And then Pam goes, no.
然后帕姆说，不是的。

1588
01:01:40.500 --> 01:01:43.560
I mean, how do you come back from hooking up with Michael?
我是说，跟迈克尔好上之后，怎么还能像以前一样相处？

1589
01:01:43.960 --> 01:01:44.300
Right.
对。

1590
01:01:44.580 --> 01:01:46.280
And he's like, oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, Michael.
他说，哦，对，对，对，迈克尔。

1591
01:01:46.520 --> 01:01:49.500
But you see, the whole time, I feel like Jim sort of went deep.
但你看，整个过程中，我觉得吉姆想得比较深。

1592
01:01:49.500 --> 01:01:51.460
And I feel like Pam kind of stayed surface.
而我觉得帕姆还停留在表面。

1593
01:01:51.780 --> 01:01:52.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1594
01:01:52.100 --> 01:01:54.300
I don't think Pam's thinking any of that stuff at all.
我觉得帕姆根本没往那方面想。

1595
01:01:54.400 --> 01:01:57.940
She's really thinking, Jan hooked up with Michael.
她真的只是在想，简竟然和迈克尔好上了。

1596
01:01:58.180 --> 01:01:58.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1597
01:01:58.800 --> 01:01:59.160
Michael.
迈克尔。

1598
01:01:59.440 --> 01:01:59.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1599
01:01:59.740 --> 01:02:01.400
She's not thinking office romances.
她没在想办公室恋情的事。

1600
01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:04.800
But it's just a little moment for me that kind of broke my heart.
但这对我来说只是一个小瞬间，却让我有点心碎。

1601
01:02:04.800 --> 01:02:08.480
And it's kind of like what Larry is talking about, that at the heart, it's a romantic
这有点像拉里所说的那样，本质上，这是一部浪漫

1602
01:02:08.480 --> 01:02:09.600
comedy, you know?
喜剧，你懂吗？

1603
01:02:09.800 --> 01:02:12.400
And Jim is thinking about Pam.
吉姆在想帕姆。

1604
01:02:12.540 --> 01:02:19.120
And so when he realizes Pam hasn't even clocked that, you know, that he's thinking about them
所以当他意识到帕姆甚至都没察觉到，你知道，他想的那些事

1605
01:02:19.120 --> 01:02:21.240
in a way that she's not even thinking about in that moment.
是她在那一刻根本没想到的。

1606
01:02:21.440 --> 01:02:23.880
Jan then says she is heading back to New York.
简随后说她要回纽约了。

1607
01:02:24.040 --> 01:02:28.540
And there's this big scene where Michael chases her to the elevator.
然后有一场重头戏，迈克尔追着她到了电梯口。

1608
01:02:28.540 --> 01:02:32.900
Oh, Jenna, before we get into that scene, I just have one little comment about something
哦，珍娜，在我们进入那场戏之前，我只想对背景里的某个东西

1609
01:02:32.900 --> 01:02:33.420
in the background.
发表一个小评论。

1610
01:02:33.560 --> 01:02:34.060
What is it?
是什么？

1611
01:02:34.280 --> 01:02:38.520
At 19 minutes, eight seconds, you guys, as Jan is leaving the building and Michael's chasing
在19分08秒的时候，大家，当简离开大楼而迈克尔在后面追她时，

1612
01:02:38.520 --> 01:02:42.800
after her, you really get a great look at the Dunder Mifflin sign.
你们真的能很清楚地看到邓德·米夫林的招牌。

1613
01:02:43.240 --> 01:02:43.780
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1614
01:02:44.020 --> 01:02:44.800
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1615
01:02:44.940 --> 01:02:49.380
You probably think that sign is like made of something hard and sturdy, right?
你们可能觉得那块招牌是用某种坚硬结实的材料做的，对吧？

1616
01:02:49.600 --> 01:02:52.940
Doesn't it look like plastic or something?
看起来像塑料之类的东西，对吗？

1617
01:02:53.140 --> 01:02:53.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1618
01:02:53.640 --> 01:02:54.120
Composite?
复合材料？

1619
01:02:54.260 --> 01:02:55.660
It's foam board.
那是泡沫板。

1620
01:02:56.180 --> 01:02:56.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1621
01:02:56.480 --> 01:02:56.540
Yeah.
没错。

1622
01:02:57.200 --> 01:02:59.060
It's like almost like a craft project.
简直就像个手工课作业。

1623
01:02:59.300 --> 01:03:02.200
It's almost like a poster you would make for your kid's third grade project.
几乎就像你为你孩子三年级作业做的海报一样。

1624
01:03:02.460 --> 01:03:06.160
I remember we would have scenes where we'd have to line up and come in and out of the
我记得我们拍戏时得排队进出

1625
01:03:06.160 --> 01:03:06.500
office.
办公室。

1626
01:03:06.540 --> 01:03:09.300
And we'd be stuck back there in that little corner off camera.
我们会被困在镜头外的那个小角落里。

1627
01:03:09.380 --> 01:03:11.060
And you could just push on it.
你可以直接推它。

1628
01:03:11.260 --> 01:03:13.100
And it was just like foam board.
它真的就是泡沫板。

1629
01:03:13.720 --> 01:03:19.900
Well, I used to remember being worried for it because it did feel very precarious.
嗯，我记得我以前很担心它，因为它感觉非常不稳。

1630
01:03:20.040 --> 01:03:22.460
Like if your elbow might go right through it.
就像你的手肘可能会直接戳穿它一样。

1631
